01:37:33.900 --> 01:37:36.248
I'm sure Chris would have
something to say on this,

01:37:36.248 --> 01:37:39.930
just the point that
Mary, around education,

01:37:39.930 --> 01:37:41.940
we have had conversations with the Academy

01:37:41.940 --> 01:37:44.820
of Medical Royal Colleges
to look initially

01:37:44.820 --> 01:37:46.861
at the postgraduate curriculum,

01:37:46.861 --> 01:37:49.320
but hoping that we will be able to go

01:37:49.320 --> 01:37:51.204
further upstream than that.

01:37:51.204 --> 01:37:53.460
'Cause I don't remember being
taught in medical school

01:37:53.460 --> 01:37:55.020
that maybe the reason why my patient's

01:37:55.020 --> 01:37:56.130
blood pressure isn't going down

01:37:56.130 --> 01:37:57.969
is that they can't afford the medications

01:37:57.969 --> 01:38:00.660
and therefore we're having
the conversations with them

01:38:00.660 --> 01:38:03.420
about what might we be able
to do with the curriculum

01:38:03.420 --> 01:38:05.850
that starts to expand
people's understanding

01:38:05.850 --> 01:38:08.310
of those wider determinants and yes,

01:38:08.310 --> 01:38:11.250
oral health and how we
could have positioned

01:38:11.250 --> 01:38:13.030
that within a prevention space.

01:38:13.030 --> 01:38:16.800
We did an extensive
co-production with stakeholders

01:38:16.800 --> 01:38:19.080
in arriving at those five clinical areas.

01:38:19.080 --> 01:38:20.490
And yes, you're right,

01:38:20.490 --> 01:38:22.560
