diversifying education,

01:39:14.610 --> 01:39:16.350
which is one of our work streams.

01:39:16.350 --> 01:39:18.420
And in fact the very first piece of work

01:39:18.420 --> 01:39:20.760
that we did in the observatory
looking at racial bias

01:39:20.760 --> 01:39:23.520
and pulse oximetry raised
a number of questions.

01:39:23.520 --> 01:39:26.970
The number of clinicians that
came to us actually and said,

01:39:26.970 --> 01:39:30.030
we weren't taught that when
we were in medical school

01:39:30.030 --> 01:39:31.980
was quite significant.

01:39:31.980 --> 01:39:33.780
- And if I may say in nursing school.

01:39:33.780 --> 01:39:35.640
- And nursing school, absolutely.

01:39:35.640 --> 01:39:38.970
And so it's about what gets taught,

01:39:38.970 --> 01:39:41.040
what doesn't get taught,
what features in textbooks,

01:39:41.040 --> 01:39:42.600
what doesn't feature
in text and skin colour

01:39:42.600 --> 01:39:43.890
is one of those things.

01:39:43.890 --> 01:39:46.200
So that piece of work actually led

01:39:46.200 --> 01:39:49.320
to the Margaret Whitehead review,

01:39:49.320 --> 01:39:50.310
which is ongoing at the moment,

01:39:50.310 --> 01:39:52.080
looking at equity in medical devices

01:39:52.080 --> 01:39:53.857
and that will have an impact, yes,

01:39:53.857 --> 01:39:56.460
on medical devices
assessments and testing,

01:39:56.460 --> 01:39:59.490
but also hopefully on
education and what gets taught

01:39:59.490 --> 01:40:00.960
around those as well.

