01:42:15.450 --> 01:42:18.240
That's one of the things we're working

01:42:18.240 --> 01:42:19.743
with partners to do at the moment.

01:42:19.743 --> 01:42:22.200
Two the questions that have been asked.

01:42:22.200 --> 01:42:23.700
I think what we've got here

01:42:23.700 --> 01:42:26.220
is we've got an approach that works.

01:42:26.220 --> 01:42:28.650
So the Core20PLUS5 approach works

01:42:28.650 --> 01:42:29.750
at a number of levels.

01:42:30.595 --> 01:42:32.225
We've get great examples
of where it works locally

01:42:32.225 --> 01:42:36.050
and the fact that it is so much a

01:42:36.050 --> 01:42:38.220
kind of bottom up endeavour

01:42:38.220 --> 01:42:39.422
as it were

01:42:39.422 --> 01:42:40.860
is is exactly as it should be

01:42:40.860 --> 01:42:43.110
because it is about local teams

01:42:43.110 --> 01:42:46.110
understanding local populations,
working in partnership

01:42:46.110 --> 01:42:48.570
and doing things that are
going to make a difference

01:42:48.570 --> 01:42:53.570
for their local, well their
Core20PLUS5 challenges.

01:42:55.110 --> 01:42:57.270
I think the thing that
it also works for though

01:42:57.270 --> 01:42:59.910
is as an approach it works nationally

01:42:59.910 --> 01:43:01.860
so it's completely spreadable

01:43:01.860 --> 01:43:04.236
and it applies whether you're
talking about different

01:43:04.236 --> 01:43:06.857
geographical places or
different programme approaches

01:43:06.857 --> 01:43:11.460
and what we've got, great
example lung health checks.

01:43:11.460 --> 01:43:15.339
You've mentioned already,
high intensity users work,

01:43:15.339 --> 01:43:16.230
we've talked about in the paper,

01:43:16.230 --> 01:43:20.490
the work on waiting list
inequality reduction.

01:43:20.490 --> 01:43:23.040
So we can see I think some
really concrete examples

01:43:23.040 --> 01:43:26.783
of where that approach now
it's absolutely core business

01:43:26.783 --> 01:43:29.070
for the way that it's
working nationally as well.

01:43:29.070 --> 01:43:31.200
It's always going to
be a great opportunity

01:43:31.200 --> 01:43:33.090
to take local examples of best practise

01:43:33.090 --> 01:43:34.710
and share them and spread them.

01:43:34.710 --> 01:43:36.660
And actually that is one of
the things that of course

01:43:36.660 --> 01:43:38.580
as we get more and more
evidence of impact,

01:43:38.580 --> 01:43:40.980
we can do more and more and we need to,

01:43:40.980 --> 01:43:43.590
I'm with Julian though
and Bola knows this,

01:43:43.590 --> 01:43:46.050
this conversation we've
had for at least two years,

01:43:46.050 --> 01:43:47.970
which is the, we will know

01:43:47.970 --> 01:43:51.690
we have really mainstreamed
this when every time

01:43:51.690 --> 01:43:56.010
we look at the data for
our performance reports

01:43:56.010 --> 01:43:57.390
and we do do it in the annex,

01:43:57.390 --> 01:44:00.060
but every time we look at our
core data we are looking at it

01:44:00.060 --> 01:44:02.111
through an inequalities lens

01:44:02.111 --> 01:44:03.540
as well as through the kind of aggregate

01:44:03.540 --> 01:44:07.080
and the specialty level
or whatever it lens it is.

01:44:07.080 --> 01:44:10.140
So fantastic work on the
health inequalities dashboard,

01:44:10.140 --> 01:44:11.910
but the next step is making sure

01:44:11.910 --> 01:44:13.920
that that doesn't sit,
it's a separate dashboard.

01:44:13.920 --> 01:44:16.200
It's completely embedded in
the work of the programmes.

01:44:16.200 --> 01:44:17.850
And although I don't think we are

01:44:20.350 --> 01:44:23.657
in a position necessarily
where this is the right answer.

01:44:24.850 --> 01:44:26.840
This thing that Bola and
I have also talked about

01:44:26.840 --> 01:44:28.290
is this thing about if
we did have more people,

01:44:28.290 --> 01:44:30.327
what would we do with them?

01:44:30.327 --> 01:44:31.819
And one of the things
I would definitely do

01:44:31.819 --> 01:44:33.120
with them is make sure
that you had the resource

01:44:33.120 --> 01:44:35.580
to embed in each of our programme teams

01:44:35.580 --> 01:44:38.400
so that it was very much the kind of both

01:44:38.400 --> 01:44:41.610
and both the focus that you bring,

01:44:41.610 --> 01:44:44.220
both of you actually
on the specific things

01:44:44.220 --> 01:44:47.070
that we are trying to target
and tackle through this work,

01:44:47.070 --> 01:44:51.540
the and being the bit where
every time we talk primary care,

01:44:51.540 --> 01:44:52.950
every time we talk elective,

01:44:52.950 --> 01:44:54.990
every time we talk urgent emergency care,

01:44:54.990 --> 01:44:57.630
we are just by the very
nature of how we've set it up,

01:44:57.630 --> 01:44:59.280
talking about health inequalities as well.

01:44:59.280 --> 01:45:02.297
So I do think that is how we
need to evolve our approach

01:45:02.297 --> 01:45:03.130
and we've got some great examples

01:45:03.130 --> 01:45:06.570
of where that is already
happening and paying dividends.

01:45:06.570 --> 01:45:08.010
- Amanda, thank you.

