So can we then go, Navina,

01:48:30.592 --> 01:48:33.300
I think it's the long-term workforce plan.

01:48:33.300 --> 01:48:35.550
Again, we discussed it in the
private board at some length,

01:48:35.550 --> 01:48:36.960
but I think it's really important,

01:48:36.960 --> 01:48:39.240
it's such a seminal foundation block

01:48:39.240 --> 01:48:41.280
and you've led with a number
of the exec colleagues,

01:48:41.280 --> 01:48:43.495
actually it's production and then actually

01:48:43.495 --> 01:48:45.378
with Julian's help and Amanda's help,

01:48:45.378 --> 01:48:50.213
discussing and agreeing with
government its publication,

01:48:50.213 --> 01:48:54.390
a chance here to lay the long-term

01:48:54.390 --> 01:48:56.223
workforce plan before us.

01:48:57.247 --> 01:48:58.800
- Thank you, so for the record,

01:48:58.800 --> 01:49:02.301
I want to just start by
thanking all of our partners

01:49:02.301 --> 01:49:04.980
who've worked with us
to develop this plan.

01:49:04.980 --> 01:49:07.286
So it was people within the organisation,

01:49:07.286 --> 01:49:10.890
but also a lot of stakeholders
outside of the organisation.

01:49:10.890 --> 01:49:14.040
And I'm thanking now because
we will need them to help us

01:49:14.040 --> 01:49:16.260
to deliver the plan going forward.

01:49:16.260 --> 01:49:18.180
The second thing to say is it's built

01:49:18.180 --> 01:49:20.638
on a lot of work that
has gone before this,

01:49:20.638 --> 01:49:25.638
facing the facts, people
plan, Framework 15,

01:49:26.947 --> 01:49:28.530
The People Promise,

01:49:28.530 --> 01:49:30.120
and a lot of really good work

01:49:30.120 --> 01:49:32.400
that's already been in
existence for some time.

01:49:32.400 --> 01:49:35.670
So that's a really important
point to make here.

01:49:35.670 --> 01:49:38.250
The next point I want to make
is that the three big sections

01:49:38.250 --> 01:49:42.810
for us are train, retain and reform.

01:49:42.810 --> 01:49:44.940
And actually, that applies to,

01:49:44.940 --> 01:49:47.100
I was sitting here listening
to all the conversations

01:49:47.100 --> 01:49:49.620
and I could apply train, retain, reform

01:49:49.620 --> 01:49:52.020
to health inequalities to performance,

01:49:52.020 --> 01:49:53.880
to everything that we talk about.

01:49:53.880 --> 01:49:57.888
So learning from Core20PLUS5,

01:49:57.888 --> 01:50:01.530
embedding the long-term
workforce plan, train, retain,

01:50:01.530 --> 01:50:03.960
reform at every level of everything we do

01:50:03.960 --> 01:50:06.300
is something that is part of my ambition.

01:50:06.300 --> 01:50:08.070
The final thing to say is we're now moving

01:50:08.070 --> 01:50:09.900
into delivery and implementation,

01:50:09.900 --> 01:50:12.720
which is going to be
challenging again for train,

01:50:12.720 --> 01:50:16.620
retain and reform and some
bits that we need to manage

01:50:16.620 --> 01:50:19.050
is to support many of our stakeholders

01:50:19.050 --> 01:50:24.050
for whom this change will
be quite challenging.

01:50:24.150 --> 01:50:27.300
But I do believe that if
we kind of come together

01:50:27.300 --> 01:50:29.580
and spend the time in working together

01:50:29.580 --> 01:50:32.181
to make sure that we're
talking about five,

01:50:32.181 --> 01:50:34.230
10, and 15 years and beyond,

01:50:34.230 --> 01:50:37.470
and that we have a chance
to keep looking at this

01:50:37.470 --> 01:50:39.510
because it's an iterative plan,

01:50:39.510 --> 01:50:41.640
every two years we have an opportunity

01:50:41.640 --> 01:50:43.770
to revisit and build upon it.

01:50:43.770 --> 01:50:47.550
So it's a real watershed
moment for us here

01:50:47.550 --> 01:50:49.500
in the NHS and beyond.

01:50:49.500 --> 01:50:51.630
Richard, I don't need
to say anything else.

01:50:51.630 --> 01:50:56.630
- David, would you like to
comment because you chair for us,

01:50:57.090 --> 01:50:58.800
the committee actually,

01:50:58.800 --> 01:51:00.840
which is going to engage for the board

01:51:00.840 --> 01:51:04.470
in the more direct
engagement on the rollout

01:51:04.470 --> 01:51:06.180
and the capacitization.

01:51:06.180 --> 01:51:08.890
The word I keep using and
people telling me doesn't exist,

01:51:08.890 --> 01:51:11.700
but the capacitization, it will exist

01:51:11.700 --> 01:51:14.790
I hope if I keep using
it of the workforce plan

01:51:14.790 --> 01:51:17.217
and then it will come regularly
to the board actually.

01:51:17.217 --> 01:51:19.530
- On your behalf, Richard,

01:51:19.530 --> 01:51:22.560
I'm determined to send it
into the Oxford Dictionary,

01:51:22.560 --> 01:51:26.091
ask that they consider
it for entry this year.

01:51:26.091 --> 01:51:29.850
But the day job is just to
build on what Navina said,

01:51:29.850 --> 01:51:31.311
is really to think about delivery.

01:51:31.311 --> 01:51:36.311
And this is a historic plan,
there's no doubt about that.

01:51:37.080 --> 01:51:40.620
But actually it's a plan
of many, many moving parts

01:51:40.620 --> 01:51:45.620
and so the focus that
we need to put in place

01:51:45.810 --> 01:51:47.340
on delivery is going to be critical.

01:51:47.340 --> 01:51:50.520
So on behalf of the board, the committee

01:51:50.520 --> 01:51:53.580
and colleagues on the committee
from around this table

01:51:53.580 --> 01:51:57.394
will be focused on the
delivery of that plan.

01:51:57.394 --> 01:52:00.458
I think the point about
stakeholders is also important.

01:52:00.458 --> 01:52:04.230
There are some elements
of the reform agenda,

01:52:04.230 --> 01:52:05.910
which are not without controversy,

01:52:05.910 --> 01:52:09.210
and they need a lot of stakeholder
engagements and to bring

01:52:09.210 --> 01:52:13.290
people in and we can use the
time to actually, I think,

01:52:13.290 --> 01:52:16.710
engage those wider stakeholders

01:52:16.710 --> 01:52:18.651
and partners and constituents.

01:52:18.651 --> 01:52:21.720
But I think one of the big benefits

01:52:21.720 --> 01:52:26.720
of having a multi-year
strategic workforce plan

01:52:27.240 --> 01:52:29.640
is it allows us to send
a very powerful signal,

01:52:29.640 --> 01:52:32.730
particularly to higher and
further education providers

01:52:32.730 --> 01:52:34.110
about what business we're in.

01:52:34.110 --> 01:52:36.761
And certainly the
universities and the colleges

01:52:36.761 --> 01:52:39.030
think this is a terrific piece of work

01:52:39.030 --> 01:52:40.928
because what it allows them to do

01:52:40.928 --> 01:52:43.944
is begin to plan what
investments they need to make

01:52:43.944 --> 01:52:48.020
to actually develop the
capability and the capacity.

01:52:48.020 --> 01:52:50.357
So on a campus like Aston,

01:52:50.357 --> 01:52:54.300
which does generate healthcare workers,

01:52:54.300 --> 01:52:56.250
I send in a signal about the importance

01:52:56.250 --> 01:52:58.980
of healthcare scientists,
of bioinformaticians,

01:52:58.980 --> 01:53:01.720
statisticians becomes really important

01:53:01.720 --> 01:53:04.110
because they can now start to say,

01:53:04.110 --> 01:53:07.050
actually these courses and these people

01:53:07.050 --> 01:53:08.850
are going to be funded

01:53:08.850 --> 01:53:11.130
and therefore we can
start making provision

01:53:11.130 --> 01:53:13.500
in our curriculum and our prospectuses.

01:53:13.500 --> 01:53:16.517
It won't happen for this
September, but for next September,

01:53:16.517 --> 01:53:19.170
I would expect to see
these things beginning

01:53:19.170 --> 01:53:20.610
to seep their way through.

01:53:20.610 --> 01:53:23.010
So Navina's point about
the importance of working

01:53:23.010 --> 01:53:25.650
with partners, we can't
deliver this by ourselves.

01:53:25.650 --> 01:53:27.540
We've got to deliver this in partnership

01:53:27.540 --> 01:53:32.540
with other colleagues.

01:53:32.880 --> 01:53:34.140
And I think that's a real strength

01:53:34.140 --> 01:53:35.820
of actually getting this plan out.

01:53:35.820 --> 01:53:37.107
Well, there's many real
strengths about it,

01:53:37.107 --> 01:53:38.670
but that is one of them.

01:53:38.670 --> 01:53:42.480
But I'm really focused
on behalf of the board

01:53:46.410 --> 01:53:47.790
on the delivery aspects

01:53:47.790 --> 01:53:49.590
and we get the opportunity,

01:53:49.590 --> 01:53:52.650
I think through your
champion of this agenda,

01:53:52.650 --> 01:53:55.050
Richard and Amanda's
champion of the agenda

01:53:55.050 --> 01:53:57.870
alongside Navina to bring
this on regular occasions

01:53:57.870 --> 01:54:01.107
to get the board on where
we're up to, so thank you.

01:54:01.107 --> 01:54:03.930
- Call it well delivery and capacitization

01:54:03.930 --> 01:54:07.380
at each time we do it, but Ruth, yeah.

01:54:07.380 --> 01:54:10.368
- I am interested in what the
Oxford Dictionary will say.

01:54:10.368 --> 01:54:12.720
I'm not putting any money on it, Richard.

01:54:12.720 --> 01:54:13.710
- No, nor am I.

01:54:14.907 --> 01:54:16.240
- Ruth, you want to comment I think.

01:54:16.240 --> 01:54:17.833
- Thank you very much.

01:54:17.833 --> 01:54:22.740
So this is a massive
step for my professions,

01:54:22.740 --> 01:54:25.080
nursing midwifery in particular.

01:54:25.080 --> 01:54:26.911
You know, this is huge,

01:54:26.911 --> 01:54:30.870
significant numbers of training
over the 15 year period

01:54:30.870 --> 01:54:32.655
with very detailed milestones.

01:54:32.655 --> 01:54:37.655
It's been very welcomed,
the retained part of it.

01:54:37.789 --> 01:54:39.360
We're going to need to do that now.

01:54:39.360 --> 01:54:42.540
That's an urgent one
for every organisation.

01:54:42.540 --> 01:54:46.498
If we're going to deliver
the winter plan this year,

01:54:46.498 --> 01:54:48.900
the delivery of retention

01:54:48.900 --> 01:54:50.640
is going to be really important.

01:54:50.640 --> 01:54:53.970
The reform, I'm just really pleased

01:54:53.970 --> 01:54:56.880
to see the commitment to continuing

01:54:56.880 --> 01:54:59.306
graduate professions for
nursing and midwifery.

01:54:59.306 --> 01:55:03.030
Welcome the continuation

01:55:03.030 --> 01:55:04.980
of the undergraduate three year course

01:55:04.980 --> 01:55:07.107
and the postgraduate two year course.

01:55:07.107 --> 01:55:10.269
But I particularly welcome
the apprenticeship model.

01:55:10.269 --> 01:55:14.520
These people that going to
do the apprenticeship model,

01:55:14.520 --> 01:55:16.680
it's about widening access.

01:55:16.680 --> 01:55:19.380
It's about, they come out
with exactly the same degree,

01:55:19.380 --> 01:55:23.400
exactly the same quality
achievements at the end of it.

01:55:23.400 --> 01:55:25.080
And I, for one and going to stand

01:55:25.080 --> 01:55:28.500
very much behind all of those models,

01:55:28.500 --> 01:55:30.943
not favouring one or the other,

01:55:30.943 --> 01:55:32.910
but it's important to back all of them.

01:55:32.910 --> 01:55:35.520
So yeah, let's get on and deliver it.

01:55:35.520 --> 01:55:36.960
- Thank you, Mary.

01:55:36.960 --> 01:55:40.140
- I wanted to say that
I'm particularly delighted

01:55:40.140 --> 01:55:42.270
that you've got to this point

01:55:42.270 --> 01:55:46.530
because we have got a global
shortage of healthcare workers.

01:55:46.530 --> 01:55:49.860
And I know that the
World Health Organisation

01:55:49.860 --> 01:55:52.620
see this particular strategy

01:55:52.620 --> 01:55:57.480
as an exemplar for other
western countries in particular.

01:55:57.480 --> 01:55:59.310
Because if we're going to have

01:55:59.310 --> 01:56:02.160
a globally safe healthcare world,

01:56:02.160 --> 01:56:05.683
we cannot continue to
recruit internationally.

01:56:05.683 --> 01:56:08.460
We must not only grow our own,

01:56:08.460 --> 01:56:10.355
but enable some of them to go

01:56:10.355 --> 01:56:12.120
and get international
experience and come back.

01:56:12.120 --> 01:56:15.741
So just really wanted to
recognise the importance of that.

01:56:15.741 --> 01:56:19.980
- Very good, Amanda have
the last words on it,

01:56:19.980 --> 01:56:22.004
but actually engaging on it,

01:56:22.004 --> 01:56:24.480
it was a remarkable exercise in many ways

01:56:24.480 --> 01:56:27.510
because it required us to envision

01:56:27.510 --> 01:56:29.500
what the health service might look like

01:56:30.570 --> 01:56:32.490
in five years, 10 years, 15 years,

01:56:32.490 --> 01:56:34.800
including skills mix
changes and how technology

01:56:34.800 --> 01:56:35.880
would play in

01:56:35.880 --> 01:56:38.670
the point about international recruitment,

01:56:38.670 --> 01:56:41.610
we got wonderful international
recruits, wonderful recruits,

01:56:41.610 --> 01:56:43.237
but the strategic
vulnerability of over reliance

01:56:43.237 --> 01:56:46.500
on an international supply chain

01:56:46.500 --> 01:56:49.380
when it's highly competitive
is clearly something

01:56:49.380 --> 01:56:52.573
that needed to be reflected
in as one of its factors.

01:56:52.573 --> 01:56:54.661
And I agree, it's a huge step forward,

01:56:54.661 --> 01:56:57.600
I think, to have this plan.

01:56:57.600 --> 01:57:00.210
And I also think the fact it gets reviewed

01:57:00.210 --> 01:57:02.880
and sort of moderated every two years,

01:57:02.880 --> 01:57:05.550
reflected on to keep it
live, keep it relevant,

01:57:05.550 --> 01:57:08.400
because we also all know
that there's assumptions

01:57:08.400 --> 01:57:10.200
about what we might look
like in 15 years time

01:57:10.200 --> 01:57:12.237
are probably unlikely to be quite right.

01:57:12.237 --> 01:57:15.000
And so we do need to keep
adjusting and amending.

01:57:15.000 --> 01:57:17.770
But Amanda, do you want to
have the last words on it?

01:57:17.770 --> 01:57:21.720
- Just to say, I think you're right.

01:57:21.720 --> 01:57:24.690
I think this is a really,
this is a really big moment.

01:57:24.690 --> 01:57:26.877
75 years of the NHS,

01:57:26.877 --> 01:57:29.726
this is the first time that
we've been asked by government

01:57:29.726 --> 01:57:31.659
to produce a comprehensive workforce plan.

01:57:31.659 --> 01:57:33.990
And crucially, government
has fully backed it.

01:57:33.990 --> 01:57:35.041
- Yeah.

01:57:35.041 --> 01:57:37.451
- Including with funding for the education

01:57:37.451 --> 01:57:38.940
and training element
for the next five years.

01:57:38.940 --> 01:57:41.610
So it's not just a piece
of paper, this is real.

01:57:41.610 --> 01:57:44.010
And I completely agree for all the work

01:57:44.010 --> 01:57:45.540
that's gone into getting us here,

01:57:45.540 --> 01:57:49.080
it's the delivery, not the capacitization,

01:57:49.080 --> 01:57:50.283
it's the delivery.

01:57:52.408 --> 01:57:54.086
- It will be there.

01:57:54.086 --> 01:57:57.330
- That now takes centre stage,
and exactly as Navina says,

01:57:57.330 --> 01:57:59.760
the importance for me is
it's those three elements

01:57:59.760 --> 01:58:01.620
and Ruth is right.

01:58:01.620 --> 01:58:03.596
It's here now on retention.

01:58:03.596 --> 01:58:07.830
Because that's the bit that
we've absolutely recognised

01:58:07.830 --> 01:58:10.650
is going to have the
most immediate impact.

01:58:10.650 --> 01:58:14.610
But the fact that we can
have some real credible hope

01:58:14.610 --> 01:58:19.080
for the future on reform
and also on the numbers

01:58:19.080 --> 01:58:20.610
and skills of people coming through,

01:58:20.610 --> 01:58:22.080
reforming the way that we do it,

01:58:22.080 --> 01:58:24.000
as well as the roles that they come into

01:58:24.000 --> 01:58:25.950
alongside those traditional routes

01:58:25.950 --> 01:58:28.770
I think is absolutely critical.

01:58:28.770 --> 01:58:30.810
- Very good, so thank you.

01:58:30.810 --> 01:58:32.910
I think that's the last
item for the board.

01:58:32.910 --> 01:58:35.160
So I'll just pause for a moment

01:58:35.160 --> 01:58:37.292
to see if there's any other business

01:58:37.292 --> 01:58:38.760
that anyone wants to raise.

01:58:38.760 --> 01:58:40.200
And if not, thank you very much,

01:58:40.200 --> 01:58:42.060
I'll call the board to close.

01:58:42.060 --> 01:58:43.950
So thank you very much everybody.

01:58:43.950 --> 01:58:46.180
And we had the dinner tonight
with about 15 local leaders,

01:58:46.180 --> 01:58:50.913
16 or 17 I think local leaders
from Birmingham and Solihull.

